  "excerpt": "[docs/resource-guides/gcp/database.md#cloud-sql-type-database]\npskit's Cloud Functions don't run in a VPC, so the simplest path is a **public IP** instance reached through the **Cloud SQL Python Connector**: it authenticates with the function's service account and encrypts the connection, with no authorized networks to open. A private-IP-only instance needs a Serverless VPC Access connector, added as shown in [cache.md](cache.md#3-declare-it-in-pskityml).",
  "provider": "gcp",
  "stage": "staging",
  "mode": "ask",
